{"id":"mve7u3o9-dxcgnl","dreamId":"mve7tc04-8kywog","season":1,"number":2,"stage":2,"title":"After the Wanting","revision":1,"writtenAt":"2026-10-18T19:25:50.746Z","source":"migrated-v1","wovenProofId":null,"opening":{"morning":{"key":"p0","fragmentId":"v1:op7","beat":"opening","text":"The day doesn't ask anything of you yet. It just waits, warm and unhurried, while you remember who you've become.","spans":[]},"evening":{"key":"p0","fragmentId":"v1:op7","beat":"opening","text":"The day doesn't ask anything of you yet. It just waits, warm and unhurried, while you remember who you've become.","spans":[]}},"body":[{"key":"p1","fragmentId":"v1:ar-ca2","beat":"arrival","text":"The first task of the day is one you'd do for free — and they pay you well for it. Strange and wonderful, how the intention held: my own design studio, with clients who trust my eye.","spans":[]},{"key":"p2","fragmentId":"v1:se3","beat":"sensory","text":"The air outside smells faintly of rain that already fell. Everything is rinsed, including — somehow — you.","spans":[]},{"key":"p3","fragmentId":"v1:li-ca3","beat":"living","text":"You decline a shiny thing that isn't yours to do, and the calendar breathes. Mastery is mostly subtraction, you've learned.","spans":[]},{"key":"p4","fragmentId":"v1:wi7","beat":"living","text":"Someone younger watches how you move through the day and quietly adjusts their own sails. You remember being them. You'd have loved proof like you.","spans":[]},{"key":"p5","fragmentId":"v1:gr6","beat":"reflection","text":"Somewhere in the day you feel it land — that this was once the dream. This exact, ordinary, extraordinary Tuesday. You feel proud, all the way through.","spans":[]},{"key":"p6","fragmentId":"v1:proof-2","beat":"recall","text":"There is proof behind this memory now: Sent my portfolio to two studios I admire. It is small enough to be real, and real enough to change what comes next.","spans":[]}],"closing":{"morning":{"key":"p7","fragmentId":"v1:cl2","beat":"closing","text":"You set tomorrow's one intention like a cup by the kettle, then let the day go completely. Sleep comes down like warm weather.","spans":[]},"evening":{"key":"p7","fragmentId":"v1:cl2","beat":"closing","text":"You set tomorrow's one intention like a cup by the kettle, then let the day go completely. Sleep comes down like warm weather.","spans":[]}},"wordCount":{"morning":196,"evening":196},"engineVersion":1}